{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and accepted.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment's pod template had a `service-route: frontend` label added in its revision 2 rollout. The `frontend` Service selects on that label, so it was routing traffic to the `search` pod as well. The `search` pod doesn't listen on port 5000, so roughly 30% of requests through the Service failed with connection refused.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the `service-route` label from the `search` deployment's pod template with a JSON patch. The `frontend` Service now has only the frontend pod as an endpoint, and 200 of 200 test requests through `frontend:5000` succeeded at about 76 ms average.\n\nI submitted once with an empty solution string, as instructed. I haven't seen the grader's result beyond the acceptance message."}}
